  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Original whole organism: broad torso, upright long neck, extremely long hand claws. Not isolated claw, raptor or movie character. [\"Head, neck and trunk proportions are family-based reconstruction; colour, feathers/skin and keratin tips not directly preserved for this specimen.\", \"No claim that claws definitely killed prey, dug soil or pulled plants; functions remain debated.\", \"No blindness or movie-specific ornament.\"] {\"body_length_m\": 10.0, \"basis\": \"NHM species estimate, not measured complete individual. NHM says 50 cm hand claws without an explicit bone-versus-sheath measurement protocol; keratin extension uncertain.\", \"standing_bounds_blender_m\": {\"min\": [-1.5082985162734985, -3.13405442237854, 0.0], \"max\": [1.5082985162734985, 4.30108642578125, 6.18284273147583], \"size\": [3.016597032546997, 7.43514084815979, 6.18284273147583]}, \"bounds_note\": \"The 10 m museum value describes estimated anatomical length, not this upright posed bounding box. Neither soft tissue nor whole-body dimensions are claimed to be directly measured fossils.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：Original whole organism: broad torso, upright long neck, extremely long hand claws. Not isolated claw, raptor or movie character. [\"Head, neck and trunk proportions are family-based reconstruction; colour, feathers/skin and keratin tips not directly preserved for this specimen.\", \"No claim that claws definitely killed prey, dug soil or pulled plants; functions remain debated.\", \"No blindness or movie-specific ornament.\"] {\"body_length_m\": 10.0, \"basis\": \"NHM species estimate, not measured complete individual. NHM says 50 cm hand claws without an explicit bone-versus-sheath measurement protocol; keratin extension uncertain.\", \"standing_bounds_blender_m\": {\"min\": [-1.5082985162734985, -3.13405442237854, 0.0], \"max\": [1.5082985162734985, 4.30108642578125, 6.18284273147583], \"size\": [3.016597032546997, 7.43514084815979, 6.18284273147583]}, \"bounds_note\": \"The 10 m museum value describes estimated anatomical length, not this upright posed bounding box. Neither soft tissue nor whole-body dimensions are claimed to be directly measured fossils.\"}"
  },
